From: Mason Chang <mason-cw.chang@mediatek.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:04:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: remove netsys v1 restriction for
 small frag check

All TX DMAs across all Netsys versions have a hardware limitation that
SDL must not be less than 16, so the Netsys version check has to be
removed.

Without this patch, the TX DMA may behave unexpectedly when processing
fragments shorter than 16 bytes.

[Neanderfunk: aus mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds 241d864218630c9cb380a3657c89f8fc3bdc3434
 (dort 25.12/patches-6.12/999-eth-56) auf OpenWrts
 generic/pending-6.6/732-01 (Kernel 6.6) uebertragen. In 6.6 steht die
 netsys-v1-Bedingung direkt in mtk_start_xmit statt in mtk_skb_valid_gso.]
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -1788,8 +1788,7 @@
 		return NETDEV_TX_BUSY;
 	}
 
-	if (mtk_is_netsys_v1(eth) &&
-	    skb_is_gso(skb) && mtk_skb_has_small_frag(skb)) {
+	if (skb_is_gso(skb) && mtk_skb_has_small_frag(skb)) {
 		segs = skb_gso_segment(skb, dev->features & ~NETIF_F_ALL_TSO);
 		if (IS_ERR(segs))
 			goto drop;
@@ -1816,8 +1815,7 @@
 	}
 
 	skb_list_walk_safe(skb, skb, next) {
-		if ((mtk_is_netsys_v1(eth) &&
-		     mtk_skb_has_small_frag(skb) && skb_linearize(skb)) ||
+		if ((mtk_skb_has_small_frag(skb) && skb_linearize(skb)) ||
 		    mtk_tx_map(skb, dev, tx_num, ring, gso) < 0) {
 				stats->tx_dropped++;
 				dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
